/* =====================================================================
   Refractory / Unexplained Chronic Cough (RCC) — QSP Mechanistic Map
   Cough Hypersensitivity Syndrome
   ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   THE ORGANISING IDEA

     CHRONIC COUGH IS NOT A SYMPTOM OF SOMETHING ELSE.
     IT IS A DISORDER OF THE COUGH REFLEX ARC ITSELF.

   For fifty years chronic cough was managed as a search for a cause —
   asthma, reflux, post-nasal drip — and treated by treating the cause.
   That paradigm fails in roughly 20-40% of specialist-clinic patients,
   and it fails in a specific and informative way: the "causes" get
   treated, the objective evidence of them disappears, and the cough
   does not. Inhaled corticosteroids do nothing without eosinophils.
   Proton-pump inhibitors do nothing without acid. Both are on this map
   precisely so that the model can reproduce their FAILURE.

   The modern reframing (Chung, Morice, McGarvey, Mazzone, Undem) is
   that refractory chronic cough is a NEUROPATHIC disorder of the vagal
   reflex arc, the airway analogue of neuropathic pain, with the same
   two hallmark abnormalities:

       HYPERTUSSIA  exaggerated cough to a tussive stimulus  (hyperalgesia)
       ALLOTUSSIA   cough to a stimulus that should not evoke it, e.g.
                    talking, laughing, cold air, aerosol, perfume   (allodynia)

   plus LARYNGEAL PARAESTHESIA — the "tickle" — which is the airway
   equivalent of spontaneous neuropathic pain and which, crucially,
   arises from ECTOPIC AFFERENT DISCHARGE, i.e. from the nerve itself
   rather than from anything in the airway. A patient can cough with a
   completely normal airway.

   ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   THE THREE LAYERS, AND WHY THE MAP IS DRAWN THIS WAY

     LAYER 1  PERIPHERAL GAIN  (what the airway does to the nerve)
              epithelial damage -> pannexin-1 -> extracellular ATP
              -> P2X3 homotrimers on vagal C-fibre terminals; plus
              NGF/TrkA, PGE2/EP3, bradykinin/B2 and acid/ASIC
              sensitising TRPV1 and TRPA1 and up-regulating P2X3 itself.
              This is the layer every P2X3 antagonist acts on.

     LAYER 2  CENTRAL GAIN  (what the nerve does to the brainstem)
              sustained afferent barrage -> nTS second-order neuron
              NMDA-dependent WIND-UP, substance P/NK-1, loss of
              GABA/glycinergic inhibition, microglial BDNF. This is the
              layer that makes the disorder OUTLIVE ITS TRIGGER, and it
              is the layer gabapentin, pregabalin, morphine and
              amitriptyline act on.

     LAYER 3  CORTICAL CONTROL  (what the person does about it)
              Cough is unique among airway reflexes in being under
              conscious control. Afferent drive first becomes the
              conscious URGE TO COUGH (insula/ACC), and only then, if
              descending prefrontal suppression is insufficient, a
              motor cough. This layer is why speech-and-language
              therapy works, why cough is near-abolished during sleep,
              and — the single most important fact for anyone designing
              a cough trial — why the PLACEBO RESPONSE IN OBJECTIVE
              COUGH COUNTS IS ~30%.

   ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   THE VICIOUS CIRCLE (bold red edges on the map)

     afferent barrage -> nTS wind-up -> central gain -> more cough
     -> laryngeal mechanical trauma -> epithelial damage -> ATP
     -> afferent barrage

   Above a critical loop gain this circle is SELF-SUSTAINING: remove the
   original insult and the cough persists. Below it, the same insult
   produces a post-viral cough that resolves in 8 weeks. In the
   accompanying mrgsolve model the disease is GENERATED by this
   bistability rather than assumed — a single insult amplitude decides
   whether the virtual patient recovers or becomes refractory.

   ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   THE CENTRAL PHARMACOLOGICAL CLAIM OF THIS MAP

   Four P2X3 antagonists have been taken into phase 2b/3 chronic cough
   trials. They share ONE efficacy mechanism and differ in ONE number —
   selectivity for the homotrimeric P2X3 receptor on vagal afferents
   over the heterotrimeric P2X2/3 receptor on type II/III taste cells:

     gefapixant   selectivity ~1x     efficacy YES (modest)  taste AE 58-69%
     eliapixant   selectivity ~60x    efficacy YES (modest)  taste AE ~10-20%
                                      TERMINATED for idiosyncratic DILI
     sivopixant   selectivity ~30x    efficacy NOT confirmed taste AE ~6-13%
     camlipixant  selectivity ~1500x  efficacy YES (larger)  taste AE ~6-10%

   Efficacy and dysgeusia are therefore NOT independent for gefapixant —
   they are two readouts of the same occupancy curve, separated only by
   the selectivity ratio. The map draws them as a single drug node
   projecting to two receptor nodes, and the model reproduces all four
   compounds by changing that one parameter.

   And because the P2X3 pathway carries only part of the tussive drive,
   the class has a CEILING: complete target coverage still leaves the
   TRPV1/TRPA1/mechanical arm intact. That is why no P2X3 antagonist has
   ever produced the near-abolition of cough that morphine can.

   ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   THE DIAGNOSTIC DISSOCIATION THE MAP PREDICTS

   P2X3 antagonists strongly suppress ATP-evoked cough and barely shift
   the capsaicin C5 threshold, because capsaicin bypasses P2X3 entirely
   and gates TRPV1 directly. Both challenge outputs are drawn, and both
   are computed in the model, so this is a prediction rather than an
   assertion.

   ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   Legend
     ellipse / box        biological species, state or process
     hexagon              drug or intervention
     octagon              clinical endpoint or patient-reported outcome
     diamond              measurement / challenge test
     doubleoctagon        on-target adverse effect
     solid arrow          activation / increase
     T-bar (tee)          inhibition / decrease
     dashed               slow, transcriptional or plastic change
     bold red             the self-sustaining vicious circle
     blue                 pharmacological intervention
     orange               adverse effect / tolerability limit
   ===================================================================== */

digraph RCC_QSP {
  graph [rankdir=TB, newrank=true, splines=spline, overlap=false, nodesep=0.22,
         ranksep=0.62, fontname="Helvetica", fontsize=11,
         labelloc="t", compound=true, bgcolor="white",
         label=<<b>Refractory Chronic Cough — Cough Hypersensitivity Syndrome</b><br/>
                <font point-size="12">QSP mechanistic map · peripheral gain → central gain → cortical control · P2X3 efficacy/dysgeusia selectivity window</font>>];
  node  [fontname="Helvetica", fontsize=9, style="filled", penwidth=0.9];
  edge  [fontname="Helvetica", fontsize=8, arrowsize=0.6, penwidth=0.9, color="#555555"];

  /* ================================================================
     1. TRIGGERS AND UPSTREAM EXPOSURES
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_trig {
    label="1 · Triggers & Exposures";
    style="filled,rounded"; color="#B0BEC5"; fillcolor="#ECEFF1"; fontsize=11;
    node [shape=box, fillcolor="#CFD8DC", color="#78909C"];

    T_VIRUS   [label="Respiratory viral infection\n(rhinovirus, RSV, influenza,\nSARS-CoV-2)"];
    T_POSTVIR [label="Post-infectious cough\n(≈50% of new-onset RCC\ndates to an infection)"];
    T_ACEI    [label="ACE inhibitor\n(5-20% incidence, F>M)"];
    T_SMOKE   [label="Tobacco smoke, PM2.5,\nozone, occupational irritants"];
    T_ALLERG  [label="Inhaled allergen\n(Th2 sensitisation)"];
    T_REFLUX  [label="Gastro-oesophageal reflux\nacid + non-acid + gaseous"];
    T_UACS    [label="Upper airway cough syndrome\n(rhinosinusitis, post-nasal drip)"];
    T_IPF     [label="Parenchymal distortion\n(IPF, bronchiectasis)"];
    T_SURG    [label="Post-intubation or\npost-surgical laryngeal injury"];
    T_MENO    [label="Menopausal transition\n(oestrogen withdrawal;\nTRPV1 modulation)"];
    T_GENE    [label="Genetic predisposition\n(TRPV1 I585V, family history\nof chronic cough)"];
    T_AGE     [label="Age 55-65, female 2:1\n(lower capsaicin C5\nin women, 2-4x)"];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     2. AIRWAY EPITHELIUM AND ATP RELEASE
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_epi {
    label="2 · Airway Epithelium & ATP Release";
    style="filled,rounded"; color="#8D6E63"; fillcolor="#EFEBE9"; fontsize=11;
    node [shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#D7CCC8", color="#8D6E63"];

    EPI_INT  [label="Epithelial integrity\n(tight junctions, ZO-1,\nE-cadherin)"];
    EPI_DAM  [label="Epithelial damage\n& desquamation"];
    PANX1    [label="Pannexin-1 hemichannel\n(mechanical + inflammatory\ngating)"];
    ATP_REL  [label="Extracellular ATP release\n(airway surface liquid)"];
    ATP_ASL  [label="[ATP] in ASL\n(RCC sputum ATP ↑↑)"];
    ENTPD    [label="CD39 / CD73 ectonucleotidase\nATP → ADP → AMP → adenosine"];
    ADENO    [label="Adenosine\n(A1/A2A on afferents)"];
    MUCUS    [label="Mucus hypersecretion\nMUC5AC / MUC5B"];
    MCC      [label="Mucociliary clearance"];
    MECHSTR  [label="Mechanical shear stress\nfrom coughing itself"];
    OSMO     [label="Osmotic / hypertonic stress\n(mannitol, distilled water)"];
    EPI_REP  [label="Epithelial repair\n(EGFR, slow: weeks)"];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     3. AIRWAY INFLAMMATION AND IMMUNE CELLS
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_infl {
    label="3 · Airway Inflammation — the treatable-trait layer";
    style="filled,rounded"; color="#EF9A9A"; fillcolor="#FFEBEE"; fontsize=11;
    node [shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#FFCDD2", color="#E57373"];

    TH2      [label="Th2 / ILC2\nIL-4, IL-5, IL-13"];
    EOS      [label="Airway eosinophils\n(NAEB, cough-variant asthma)"];
    EOSPROD  [label="Eosinophil granule proteins\nECP, MBP, EPO,\neosinophil peroxidase"];
    MAST     [label="Mast cells\n(airway smooth muscle\ninfiltration)"];
    HIST     [label="Histamine → H1"];
    PGD2     [label="PGD2 → DP2 / CRTH2"];
    TRYPT    [label="Tryptase → PAR-2"];
    NEUT     [label="Neutrophils, IL-8,\nneutrophil elastase"];
    MACRO    [label="Alveolar macrophages"];
    NFKB     [label="NF-κB / MAPK\nairway inflammatory\ntranscription"];
    IL33     [label="Alarmins: IL-33, TSLP,\nIL-25"];
    FENO     [label="FeNO\n(exhaled nitric oxide)"];
    COX2     [label="COX-2 induction"];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     4. REFLUX AND LARYNGOPHARYNGEAL AXIS
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_refl {
    label="4 · Reflux & Laryngopharyngeal Axis";
    style="filled,rounded"; color="#A5D6A7"; fillcolor="#E8F5E9"; fontsize=11;
    node [shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#C8E6C9", color="#66BB6A"];

    LES      [label="Lower oesophageal\nsphincter pressure"];
    TLESR    [label="Transient LES relaxations\n(vagally mediated)"];
    ACIDREF  [label="Acid reflux\npH < 4 events"];
    NONACID  [label="Non-acid & weakly acidic\nreflux, gaseous reflux"];
    PEPSIN   [label="Pepsin & bile acids\n(laryngeal mucosal injury)"];
    ASPIRA   [label="Micro-aspiration"];
    OESVAGAL [label="Oesophago-bronchial\nvagal reflex"];
    LPR      [label="Laryngopharyngeal reflux signs\n(RSI, RFS scores)"];
    COUGHREF [label="Cough → intra-abdominal\npressure → more reflux"];
    HIATUS   [label="Hiatus hernia,\ndelayed gastric emptying"];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     5. SENSITISING MEDIATORS AND NEUROTROPHINS
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_med {
    label="5 · Sensitising Mediators & Neurotrophins";
    style="filled,rounded"; color="#FFB74D"; fillcolor="#FFF3E0"; fontsize=11;
    node [shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#FFE0B2", color="#FB8C00"];

    NGF      [label="NGF → TrkA / p75\n(↑ in RCC airway)"];
    BDNF_P   [label="BDNF (peripheral)\nartemin, GDNF"];
    PGE2     [label="PGE2 → EP3 receptor\n(the classic tussive\nprostanoid)"];
    BK       [label="Bradykinin → B2 receptor"];
    SUBP_P   [label="Substance P / CGRP / NKA\n(peripheral release,\nneurogenic inflammation)"];
    PROTON   [label="H+ / luminal acidification\n→ ASIC3, TRPV1"];
    LTD4     [label="Cysteinyl leukotriene\nCysLT → CysLT1"];
    ATPADO   [label="Purinergic signalling\nATP, UTP, adenosine"];
    IL6L     [label="IL-6 / IL-1β (local)\nneuro-immune crosstalk"];
    OXSTR    [label="Oxidative stress, ROS,\n4-HNE (TRPA1 agonist)"];
    ESTRO    [label="Oestrogen / progesterone\nSex steroids modulate\nTRPV1 & NGF"];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     6. ION CHANNELS AND RECEPTORS ON VAGAL AFFERENT TERMINALS
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_chan {
    label="6 · Afferent Terminal Ion Channels & Receptors";
    style="filled,rounded"; color="#7986CB"; fillcolor="#E8EAF6"; fontsize=11;
    node [shape=box, style="filled,rounded", fillcolor="#C5CAE9", color="#5C6BC0"];

    P2X3     [label="P2X3 homotrimer\n(jugular/nodose C-fibre)\nATP-gated cation channel"];
    P2X23    [label="P2X2/3 heterotrimer\n(slowly desensitising)"];
    P2X3EXP  [label="P2X3 up-regulation\n(NGF-driven, DAYS-WEEKS)"];
    TRPV1    [label="TRPV1\ncapsaicin, H+, heat,\nanandamide, 12-HPETE"];
    TRPA1    [label="TRPA1\nacrolein, cinnamaldehyde,\n4-HNE, cold"];
    TRPM8    [label="TRPM8\ncold, menthol\n(ANTI-tussive when activated)"];
    ASIC3    [label="ASIC3\nacid-sensing ion channel"];
    NAV17    [label="Nav1.7 / Nav1.8 / Nav1.9\naction potential initiation\nand conduction"];
    KV       [label="Kv7 / KCa channels\nmembrane stabilisation\n(brake on excitability)"];
    NK1P     [label="NK-1 / NK-2 (peripheral)"];
    B2R      [label="B2 bradykinin receptor"];
    EP3R     [label="EP3 prostanoid receptor"];
    A2CH     [label="α2δ-1 subunit\n(Ca_v accessory, up-regulated\nin neuropathic states)"];
    MOR_P    [label="μ-opioid receptor\n(peripheral terminals)"];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     7. VAGAL AFFERENT SUBTYPES
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_aff {
    label="7 · Vagal Afferent Subtypes";
    style="filled,rounded"; color="#4DB6AC"; fillcolor="#E0F2F1"; fontsize=11;
    node [shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#B2DFDB", color="#26A69A"];

    JUG_C    [label="Jugular C-fibre\n(neural-crest derived)\nTRPV1+, P2X3+, TAC1+\n→ URGE + cough"];
    NOD_C    [label="Nodose C-fibre\n(placode derived)\nP2X2/3+, 5-HT3+"];
    AD_COUGH [label="Nodose Aδ 'cough receptor'\nlow-threshold mechanosensor,\nacid-sensitive, P2X3+\n→ the classic cough afferent"];
    RAR      [label="RAR / SAR\nrapidly & slowly adapting\nstretch receptors"];
    SLN      [label="Superior laryngeal nerve (SLN)\nlaryngeal mucosal afferents"];
    EXTRAP   [label="Extrapulmonary afferents\nnasal, pharyngeal, oesophageal,\nauricular (Arnold's) branch"];
    AFIRE    [label="Integrated afferent\nfiring rate (Hz)"];
    ECTOPIC  [label="ECTOPIC spontaneous discharge\n→ laryngeal paraesthesia,\nthe 'tickle' with a normal airway"];
    PERIPHSENS [label="PERIPHERAL SENSITISATION\nlowered activation threshold,\nrecruitment of silent afferents"];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     8. BRAINSTEM: nTS SECOND-ORDER PROCESSING
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_nts {
    label="8 · Brainstem nTS Second-Order Processing";
    style="filled,rounded"; color="#BA68C8"; fillcolor="#F3E5F5"; fontsize=11;
    node [shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#E1BEE7", color="#AB47BC"];

    NTS      [label="Nucleus tractus solitarius (nTS)\n2nd-order relay neurons"];
    NMDA     [label="NMDA-R (GluN2B)\nMg2+ block relief"];
    AMPA     [label="AMPA / kainate\nfast glutamatergic\ntransmission"];
    SUBP_C   [label="Substance P → NK-1\n(central terminals)\nslow depolarisation"];
    GABAI    [label="GABA_A / glycinergic\ninhibitory interneurons\n(the brake)"];
    MICROG   [label="Microglial activation\np38 MAPK, BDNF release"];
    ASTRO    [label="Astrocyte glutamate\nre-uptake (GLT-1)"];
    WINDUP   [label="Wind-up\nCENTRAL SENSITISATION\nuse-dependent amplification\nof synaptic gain"];
    PSNEUR   [label="Paratrigeminal nucleus (Pa5)\njugular C-fibre relay\n→ urge/affective route"];
    CVLM     [label="Caudal VLM / RVLM\nrespiratory pattern\nintegration"];
    SEROT    [label="5-HT3 / 5-HT2A\nserotonergic modulation"];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     9. DESCENDING MODULATION
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_desc {
    label="9 · Descending Modulation — the endogenous brake";
    style="filled,rounded"; color="#9575CD"; fillcolor="#EDE7F6"; fontsize=11;
    node [shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#D1C4E9", color="#7E57C2"];

    PAG      [label="Periaqueductal grey (PAG)"];
    RVM      [label="Rostral ventromedial medulla\nON-cells (facilitation) /\nOFF-cells (inhibition)"];
    RAPHE    [label="Raphe\nSerotonergic descending"];
    LC       [label="Locus coeruleus (LC)\nnoradrenergic → α2"];
    ENKEPH   [label="Endogenous opioids\nEnkephalin / β-endorphin\n→ μ, δ, κ receptors"];
    DESCINH  [label="DESCENDING INHIBITORY TONE\n(reduced in RCC and by\nsleep deprivation)"];
    DESCFAC  [label="Descending facilitation\n(anxiety, catastrophising,\nhypervigilance)"];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     10. CORTICAL NETWORK AND URGE TO COUGH
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_cort {
    label="10 · Cortical Network & Urge to Cough";
    style="filled,rounded"; color="#4FC3F7"; fillcolor="#E1F5FE"; fontsize=11;
    node [shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#B3E5FC", color="#29B6F6"];

    THAL     [label="Thalamic relay (VPM)"];
    INSULA   [label="Insula\nprimary interoceptive\nrepresentation of airway"];
    ACC      [label="Anterior cingulate cortex (ACC)\naffective salience,\nunpleasantness of the urge"];
    S1       [label="Primary sensory cortex (S1/S2)\nlocalisation of the\nlaryngeal 'tickle'"];
    URGE     [label="URGE TO COUGH (Uc)\nconscious premonitory\nsensation — LOWER threshold\nthan the motor cough"];
    PFC      [label="Dorsolateral prefrontal cortex (dlPFC)\nvoluntary suppression\nnetwork"];
    CORTSUP  [label="CORTICAL SUPPRESSION CAPACITY\n— the substrate of SLT and\nof the placebo response"];
    HYPERVIG [label="Hypervigilance,\ncough catastrophising scale\n(anxiety, depression)"];
    HABIT    [label="Learned / habitual cough\nbehaviour, operant\nreinforcement"];
    ATTEN    [label="Attentional load\n(distraction reduces cough)"];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     11. COUGH MOTOR PATTERN GENERATOR AND EFFERENTS
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_motor {
    label="11 · Cough Motor Pattern Generator & Efferents";
    style="filled,rounded"; color="#FFD54F"; fillcolor="#FFFDE7"; fontsize=11;
    node [shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#FFF9C4", color="#FBC02D"];

    CPG      [label="Cough pattern generator\n(medullary respiratory\nnetwork reconfiguration)"];
    THRESH   [label="COUGH THRESHOLD\n(drive must exceed this)"];
    INSP     [label="Inspiratory phase\n(phrenic, external\nintercostals)"];
    COMPR    [label="Compressive phase\nglottic closure\n(recurrent laryngeal n.)"];
    EXPUL    [label="Expulsive phase\nabdominal + internal\nintercostal, glottal opening"];
    BOUT     [label="Cough bout structure\n(epochs, bursts,\ncoughs per bout)"];
    LARYSPAS [label="Laryngospasm & paradoxical\nvocal fold movement"];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     12. CIRCADIAN AND SLEEP GATING
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_circ {
    label="12 · Circadian & Sleep Gating";
    style="filled,rounded"; color="#90A4AE"; fillcolor="#ECEFF1"; fontsize=11;
    node [shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#CFD8DC", color="#78909C"];

    CIRCOSC  [label="Circadian oscillator\n(SCN, cortisol rhythm)"];
    AWAKE    [label="AWAKE / ASLEEP gate"];
    SLEEPSUP [label="Cough is near-ABOLISHED in\nsleep: cortical urge pathway\nis offline"];
    MORNPEAK [label="Morning post-waking peak\n(overnight secretion load\n+ reflex re-engagement)"];
    SLEEPFRAG [label="Sleep fragmentation,\ninsomnia, fatigue"];
    SLEEPDEB [label="Sleep debt degrades\ndescending inhibition"];
    AWAKEF   [label="AWAKE cough frequency\n(≈1.5x the 24-h rate)"];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     13. P2X3 ANTAGONISTS — PK/PD
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_p2x3 {
    label="13 · P2X3 Antagonists — the class";
    style="filled,rounded"; color="#42A5F5"; fillcolor="#E3F2FD"; fontsize=11;
    node [shape=hexagon, fillcolor="#BBDEFB", color="#1E88E5", fontcolor="#0D47A1"];

    GEFA     [label="Gefapixant (MK-7264)\n45 mg BID\nt½ 6.8 h · renal OAT3\nSELECTIVITY ≈ 1x\nAPPROVED JP/EU, FDA CRL"];
    CAMLI    [label="Camlipixant (BLU-5937)\n50 mg BID\nSELECTIVITY ≈ 1500x\nphase 3 CALM-1/CALM-2"];
    ELIA     [label="Eliapixant (BAY 1817080)\n75 mg BID\nSELECTIVITY ≈ 60x\nTERMINATED — idiosyncratic\nhepatotoxicity"];
    SIVO     [label="Sivopixant (S-600918)\n150-300 mg QD\nSELECTIVITY ≈ 30x\nphase 2b primary NOT met"];

    node [shape=box, style="filled,rounded", fillcolor="#E3F2FD", color="#64B5F6", fontcolor="black"];
    OCC3     [label="P2X3 homotrimer occupancy\nATP-COMPETITIVE:\nhigher airway ATP → right-shift"];
    OCC23    [label="P2X2/3 heterotrimer occupancy\n= f(C, IC50 × selectivity)"];
    CEILING  [label="CLASS CEILING\nonly ~55-60% of tussive drive\nis P2X3-dependent; TRPV1/TRPA1/\nmechanical arm is untouched"];
    RENAL    [label="Renal clearance / OAT3\ndose-adjust in CKD"];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     14. CENTRAL NEUROMODULATORS — PK/PD
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_central {
    label="14 · Central Neuromodulators";
    style="filled,rounded"; color="#5C6BC0"; fillcolor="#E8EAF6"; fontsize=11;
    node [shape=hexagon, fillcolor="#C5CAE9", color="#3949AB", fontcolor="#1A237E"];

    GABAP    [label="Gabapentin 300→1800 mg/d\nα2δ-1 ligand\nSATURABLE absorption\n(F falls with dose)"];
    PREGAB   [label="Pregabalin 75-300 mg/d\n(+ speech therapy)"];
    MORPH    [label="Morphine SR 5-10 mg BID\nμ-opioid, central"];
    NALBU    [label="Nalbuphine ER\nκ-agonist / μ-antagonist\n(IPF cough, CANAL)"];
    AMITRIP  [label="Amitriptyline 10-25 mg\nSNRI + antimuscarinic"];
    BACLO    [label="Baclofen (GABA_B)\nreduces TLESRs + central"];
    DEXTRO   [label="Dextromethorphan\nNMDA/σ1 — OTC standard,\nweak in RCC"];
    CODEINE  [label="Codeine — no better than\nplacebo in COPD cough\n(negative control)"];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     15. TREATABLE-TRAIT THERAPIES (and their informative failures)
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_trait {
    label="15 · Treatable-Trait Therapy — and its informative failures";
    style="filled,rounded"; color="#66BB6A"; fillcolor="#E8F5E9"; fontsize=11;
    node [shape=hexagon, fillcolor="#C8E6C9", color="#43A047", fontcolor="#1B5E20"];

    ICS      [label="ICS (budesonide/fluticasone)\nWORKS ONLY IF EOSINOPHILIC\n— null in true RCC"];
    LTRA     [label="Leukotriene receptor antagonist\nMontelukast\n(cough-variant asthma)"];
    PPI      [label="PPI (esomeprazole 40 mg)\nNULL without acid reflux\n— Cochrane negative"];
    PROKIN   [label="Prokinetics, alginate,\nanti-reflux surgery"];
    ANTIHIST [label="1st-gen antihistamine\n+ decongestant (UACS)"];
    NASSTER  [label="Intranasal corticosteroid,\nsaline irrigation"];
    ACEISTOP [label="ACEi withdrawal → switch to ARB\n(resolves in 1-4 weeks —\nthe cleanest peripheral cough)"];
    AZITHRO  [label="Macrolide\nAzithromycin\n(neutrophilic/bronchiectasis)"];
    BIOLOG   [label="Biologics\nAnti-IL-5 / anti-TSLP\n(eosinophilic phenotype)"];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     16. NON-PHARMACOLOGICAL THERAPY
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_nonpharm {
    label="16 · Non-Pharmacological Therapy";
    style="filled,rounded"; color="#26A69A"; fillcolor="#E0F2F1"; fontsize=11;
    node [shape=hexagon, fillcolor="#B2DFDB", color="#00897B", fontcolor="#004D40"];

    SLT      [label="Speech & language therapy\n(PSALTI: education, cough\nsuppression, breathing,\ncounselling) — LCQ +1.5"];
    CSTX     [label="Cough suppression exercises\n(sip water, swallow,\nrelaxed throat breathing)"];
    CBTC     [label="CBT for cough\ncatastrophising"];
    SLNBLOCK [label="Superior laryngeal nerve block\n(lidocaine + steroid)"];
    NEBLIDO  [label="Nebulised lidocaine /\nbenzonatate"];
    VOCALHYG [label="Vocal hygiene, hydration,\nirritant avoidance"];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     17. ON-TARGET ADVERSE EFFECTS — THE THERAPEUTIC WINDOW
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_ae {
    label="17 · On-Target Adverse Effects & the Therapeutic Window";
    style="filled,rounded"; color="#FF7043"; fillcolor="#FBE9E7"; fontsize=11;
    node [shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#FFCCBC", color="#F4511E"];

    TASTEBUD [label="Taste bud type II/III cells\nP2X2/3 = the ATP\nneurotransmitter receptor\nfor ALL five taste qualities"];
    TASTEATP [label="CALHM1/3-mediated ATP\nrelease onto gustatory\nafferent"];

    node [shape=doubleoctagon, fillcolor="#FFAB91", color="#E64A19", fontcolor="#BF360C"];
    DYSG     [label="DYSGEUSIA / AGEUSIA\ngefapixant 45 mg: 58-69%\nof patients"];
    DISCONT  [label="Taste-related discontinuation\n≈15-20% at 45 mg BID"];
    ADHERE   [label="Adherence erosion\n→ EFFECTIVENESS < EFFICACY"];
    DILI     [label="Idiosyncratic DILI\n(eliapixant — programme\nterminated)"];
    OPIOIDAE [label="Opioid adverse effects\nConstipation, sedation,\ndependence"];
    GABAAE   [label="Gabapentinoid adverse effects\nDizziness, somnolence,\nconfusion (≈31%)"];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     18. MEASUREMENT AND CHALLENGE TESTS
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_meas {
    label="18 · Measurement & Challenge Tests";
    style="filled,rounded"; color="#8E24AA"; fillcolor="#F3E5F5"; fontsize=11;
    node [shape=diamond, fillcolor="#E1BEE7", color="#8E24AA"];

    CAPSC5   [label="Capsaicin C5 threshold\n(TRPV1-mediated — BYPASSES\nP2X3, so barely shifted by\nP2X3 antagonists)"];
    ATPCHAL  [label="ATP inhalation challenge\n(P2X3-mediated — STRONGLY\nshifted by P2X3 antagonists)"];
    CITRICA  [label="Citric / tartaric acid\nchallenge (ASIC + TRPV1)"];
    COUGHMON [label="24-h objective cough monitor\n(VitaloJAK, Leicester\nCough Monitor)"];
    SPUTUM   [label="Induced sputum\ndifferential count"];
    FENOM    [label="FeNO measurement\nFeNO ≥25 ppb\n→ eosinophilic trait"];
    PHIMP    [label="24-h pH-impedance,\nHEMII, symptom association"];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     19. CLINICAL ENDPOINTS
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_endp {
    label="19 · Clinical Endpoints";
    style="filled,rounded"; color="#D32F2F"; fillcolor="#FFEBEE"; fontsize=11;
    node [shape=octagon, fillcolor="#FFCDD2", color="#C62828", fontcolor="#B71C1C"];

    CF24     [label="24-h cough frequency\n(coughs/hour, geometric mean)\nPRIMARY ENDPOINT"];
    CFAWK    [label="Awake cough frequency"];
    VAS      [label="Cough severity VAS\n0-100 mm (MCID ≈ 30 mm)"];
    LCQ      [label="Leicester Cough Questionnaire\nLCQ 3-21 (MCID 1.3)\nhealth-related QoL"];
    CSD      [label="Cough Severity Diary\nCSD 0-10 (MCID 1.3)"];
    UCSCORE  [label="Urge-to-cough score\n(mGRS 0-10)"];
    RESPOND  [label="Responder rate\n(≥1.3 LCQ, ≥30% cough\nfrequency reduction)"];
    COMPLIC  [label="Complications\nStress urinary incontinence (55%\nof women), syncope, rib fracture,\nexhaustion, social isolation"];
    DEPRESS  [label="Psychological burden\nAnxiety, depression,\nHADS ↑"];
    PLACEBO  [label="Placebo response\nPLACEBO ARM: ~30% fall in\nOBJECTIVE cough counts at 12 wk\n— the field's central\nmeasurement problem"];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     20. DISEASE-STATE INTEGRATORS
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_state {
    label="20 · Disease-State Integrators — the bistable core";
    style="filled,rounded"; color="#37474F"; fillcolor="#CFD8DC"; fontsize=11;
    node [shape=box, style="filled,bold", fillcolor="#B0BEC5", color="#263238", penwidth=2];

    PERGAIN  [label="PERIPHERAL GAIN\n(receptor expression ×\nsensitisation)"];
    CENGAIN  [label="CENTRAL GAIN\n(wind-up × loss of inhibition)"];
    LOOPGAIN [label="LOOP GAIN\n> 1 → SELF-SUSTAINING\nRefractory chronic cough\n< 1 → post-viral cough resolves"];
    HYPERSENS [label="COUGH HYPERSENSITIVITY\nhypertussia + allotussia +\nlaryngeal paraesthesia"];
    TUSSDRIVE [label="TOTAL TUSSIVE DRIVE\n= afferent barrage × central gain"];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     EDGES — 1. Triggers into the airway
     ================================================================ */
  T_VIRUS   -> EPI_DAM   [label="cytopathic"];
  T_VIRUS   -> NGF       [label="↑↑", style=dashed];
  T_VIRUS   -> T_POSTVIR;
  T_POSTVIR -> AFIRE;
  T_SMOKE   -> EPI_DAM;
  T_SMOKE   -> OXSTR;
  T_SMOKE   -> TRPA1     [label="acrolein"];
  T_ALLERG  -> TH2;
  T_REFLUX  -> ACIDREF;
  T_REFLUX  -> NONACID;
  T_UACS    -> EXTRAP    [label="pharyngeal\nafferents"];
  T_UACS    -> MUCUS;
  T_IPF     -> RAR       [label="traction on\nmechanoreceptors"];
  T_IPF     -> EPI_DAM;
  T_SURG    -> SLN;
  T_ACEI    -> BK        [label="kininase II\ninhibition"];
  T_ACEI    -> SUBP_P    [label="↓ degradation"];
  T_MENO    -> ESTRO     [style=dashed];
  T_GENE    -> TRPV1     [style=dashed, label="TRPV1 I585V"];
  T_AGE     -> PERIPHSENS [style=dashed, label="F: C5 2-4x lower"];
  T_AGE     -> CENGAIN   [style=dashed];

  /* 2. Epithelium and ATP */
  EPI_DAM  -> EPI_INT    [arrowhead=tee];
  EPI_INT  -> PANX1      [arrowhead=tee, label="intact barrier\nrestrains release"];
  EPI_DAM  -> PANX1;
  MECHSTR  -> PANX1;
  OSMO     -> PANX1;
  NFKB     -> PANX1      [style=dashed];
  PANX1    -> ATP_REL;
  EPI_DAM  -> ATP_REL    [label="lytic release"];
  ATP_REL  -> ATP_ASL;
  ENTPD    -> ATP_ASL    [arrowhead=tee];
  ATP_ASL  -> ADENO      [label="via CD39/CD73"];
  ADENO    -> AFIRE      [label="A1 excitatory"];
  ATP_ASL  -> P2X3       [label="AGONIST", penwidth=1.8, color="#1565C0"];
  ATP_ASL  -> P2X23;
  MUCUS    -> RAR        [label="mechanical"];
  MCC      -> MUCUS      [arrowhead=tee];
  MUCUS    -> MCC        [arrowhead=tee];
  EPI_REP  -> EPI_INT;
  EPI_DAM  -> EPI_REP    [style=dashed, label="slow, weeks"];
  EPI_DAM  -> MCC        [arrowhead=tee];

  /* 3. Inflammation */
  TH2      -> EOS;
  TH2      -> IL33       [dir=back];
  IL33     -> TH2;
  IL33     -> MAST;
  EOS      -> EOSPROD;
  EOSPROD  -> EPI_DAM    [label="MBP/ECP\ncytotoxicity"];
  EOS      -> NGF        [style=dashed];
  EOS      -> FENO;
  MAST     -> HIST;
  MAST     -> PGD2;
  MAST     -> TRYPT;
  HIST     -> AFIRE      [label="H1"];
  PGD2     -> AFIRE      [label="DP2"];
  TRYPT    -> PERIPHSENS [label="PAR-2"];
  NEUT     -> OXSTR;
  MACRO    -> NFKB;
  NFKB     -> IL6L;
  NFKB     -> COX2;
  COX2     -> PGE2;
  NFKB     -> NGF        [style=dashed];
  TH2      -> MUCUS      [label="IL-13"];
  OXSTR    -> TRPA1      [label="4-HNE"];
  OXSTR    -> EPI_DAM;

  /* 4. Reflux */
  LES      -> ACIDREF    [arrowhead=tee];
  TLESR    -> ACIDREF;
  TLESR    -> NONACID;
  HIATUS   -> LES        [arrowhead=tee];
  ACIDREF  -> PEPSIN;
  NONACID  -> PEPSIN;
  PEPSIN   -> LPR;
  PEPSIN   -> EPI_DAM    [label="laryngeal\nmucosal injury"];
  ACIDREF  -> PROTON;
  ASPIRA   -> EPI_DAM;
  ACIDREF  -> ASPIRA;
  ACIDREF  -> OESVAGAL;
  NONACID  -> OESVAGAL   [label="distension,\ngas"];
  OESVAGAL -> AFIRE      [label="oesophago-\nbronchial reflex"];
  LPR      -> LARYSPAS;
  LPR      -> SLN;
  COUGHREF -> ACIDREF    [color="#D32F2F", penwidth=1.5, style=bold,
                          label="cough → reflux\n→ cough"];

  /* 5. Mediators onto channels */
  NGF      -> P2X3EXP    [style=dashed, penwidth=1.6, color="#E65100",
                          label="TrkA → transcription\nDAYS-WEEKS"];
  NGF      -> TRPV1      [label="TrkA/PI3K\ntrafficking"];
  NGF      -> NAV17      [style=dashed];
  BDNF_P   -> PERIPHSENS [style=dashed];
  PGE2     -> EP3R;
  EP3R     -> TRPV1      [label="PKA\nphosphorylation"];
  EP3R     -> PERIPHSENS;
  BK       -> B2R;
  B2R      -> TRPV1      [label="PKC"];
  B2R      -> TRPA1;
  B2R      -> SUBP_P;
  PROTON   -> ASIC3;
  PROTON   -> TRPV1;
  LTD4     -> AFIRE;
  IL6L     -> PERIPHSENS;
  ESTRO    -> TRPV1      [style=dashed, label="modulates\nexpression"];
  ESTRO    -> NGF        [style=dashed];
  SUBP_P   -> NK1P;
  NK1P     -> PERIPHSENS;
  ATPADO   -> P2X3;

  /* 6. Channels into afferents */
  P2X3     -> JUG_C      [penwidth=1.6, color="#1565C0"];
  P2X3     -> AD_COUGH   [penwidth=1.6, color="#1565C0"];
  P2X23    -> NOD_C;
  P2X3EXP  -> P2X3       [label="receptor\ndensity"];
  TRPV1    -> JUG_C      [penwidth=1.4];
  TRPA1    -> JUG_C;
  ASIC3    -> AD_COUGH;
  NAV17    -> AFIRE      [label="AP generation"];
  KV       -> AFIRE      [arrowhead=tee, label="membrane\nstabilisation"];
  A2CH     -> AFIRE      [label="Ca_v traffick.,\n↑ in neuropathy"];
  MOR_P    -> AFIRE      [arrowhead=tee];
  TRPM8    -> AFIRE      [arrowhead=tee, label="menthol:\nANTI-tussive"];
  EP3R     -> AD_COUGH;
  B2R      -> JUG_C;

  /* 7. Afferents to integrated firing */
  JUG_C    -> AFIRE      [penwidth=1.5];
  NOD_C    -> AFIRE;
  AD_COUGH -> AFIRE      [penwidth=1.5];
  RAR      -> AFIRE;
  SLN      -> AFIRE      [penwidth=1.4];
  EXTRAP   -> AFIRE;
  PERIPHSENS -> AFIRE    [penwidth=1.6, label="threshold ↓"];
  PERIPHSENS -> ECTOPIC  [penwidth=1.4];
  ECTOPIC  -> AFIRE      [penwidth=1.5, label="cough with a\nnormal airway"];
  P2X3EXP  -> ECTOPIC    [style=dashed];
  NAV17    -> ECTOPIC;
  JUG_C    -> SUBP_P     [label="axon reflex"];
  JUG_C    -> PSNEUR;

  /* 8. Afferents into brainstem */
  AFIRE    -> NTS        [penwidth=2.0, color="#6A1B9A",
                          label="afferent barrage"];
  NTS      -> AMPA;
  NTS      -> NMDA;
  AFIRE    -> SUBP_C     [label="central\nrelease"];
  SUBP_C   -> NMDA       [label="NK-1 → removes\nMg2+ block"];
  NMDA     -> WINDUP     [penwidth=1.8, color="#6A1B9A"];
  AMPA     -> NTS;
  WINDUP   -> NTS        [penwidth=1.8, color="#6A1B9A", label="synaptic gain ↑"];
  GABAI    -> NTS        [arrowhead=tee, penwidth=1.4];
  WINDUP   -> GABAI      [arrowhead=tee, style=dashed,
                          label="disinhibition"];
  MICROG   -> GABAI      [arrowhead=tee, label="BDNF → KCC2 ↓"];
  AFIRE    -> MICROG     [style=dashed, label="sustained barrage,\nDAYS"];
  MICROG   -> WINDUP     [style=dashed];
  ASTRO    -> NTS        [arrowhead=tee, label="glutamate\nre-uptake"];
  WINDUP   -> ASTRO      [arrowhead=tee, style=dashed];
  SEROT    -> NTS;
  PSNEUR   -> THAL;
  NTS      -> CVLM;
  CVLM     -> CPG;
  NTS      -> THAL       [penwidth=1.4];

  /* 9. Descending modulation */
  PAG      -> RVM;
  RVM      -> DESCINH;
  RAPHE    -> DESCINH;
  LC       -> DESCINH    [label="α2-noradrenergic"];
  ENKEPH   -> DESCINH    [penwidth=1.4];
  DESCINH  -> NTS        [arrowhead=tee, penwidth=1.7, color="#4527A0",
                          label="THE BRAKE"];
  DESCINH  -> THRESH     [label="raises"];
  DESCFAC  -> NTS        [penwidth=1.3];
  HYPERVIG -> DESCFAC    [penwidth=1.4];
  PFC      -> PAG;
  SLEEPDEB -> DESCINH    [arrowhead=tee, penwidth=1.4];

  /* 10. Cortex and urge */
  THAL     -> INSULA     [penwidth=1.5];
  THAL     -> S1;
  INSULA   -> URGE       [penwidth=1.8, color="#0277BD"];
  ACC      -> URGE       [label="unpleasantness"];
  INSULA   -> ACC;
  S1       -> URGE       [label="localisation:\n'a tickle, here'"];
  URGE     -> PFC        [label="recruits\nsuppression"];
  PFC      -> CORTSUP    [penwidth=1.5];
  ATTEN    -> CORTSUP;
  CORTSUP  -> THRESH     [penwidth=1.7, color="#0277BD", label="raises threshold —\nvoluntary suppression"];
  HYPERVIG -> CORTSUP    [arrowhead=tee];
  HYPERVIG -> URGE       [label="amplifies\npercept"];
  URGE     -> HYPERVIG   [style=dashed];
  HABIT    -> CPG        [label="operant\nreinforcement"];
  URGE     -> HABIT      [style=dashed];
  URGE     -> UCSCORE;

  /* 11. Motor output */
  TUSSDRIVE -> CPG       [penwidth=2.0, color="#C62828"];
  THRESH   -> CPG        [arrowhead=tee, penwidth=1.7];
  AFIRE    -> TUSSDRIVE  [penwidth=1.6];
  CENGAIN  -> TUSSDRIVE  [penwidth=1.6];
  CPG      -> INSP;
  INSP     -> COMPR;
  COMPR    -> EXPUL;
  EXPUL    -> BOUT;
  CPG      -> BOUT;
  LARYSPAS -> CPG;
  EXPUL    -> MECHSTR    [color="#D32F2F", penwidth=1.8, style=bold,
                          label="cough traumatises\nthe airway"];
  EXPUL    -> COUGHREF   [color="#D32F2F", penwidth=1.5, style=bold];

  /* 12. Circadian and sleep */
  CIRCOSC  -> AWAKE      [penwidth=1.4];
  AWAKE    -> CORTSUP    [label="suppression only\nexists when awake"];
  AWAKE    -> CPG        [penwidth=1.6, label="GATE"];
  SLEEPSUP -> CPG        [arrowhead=tee, penwidth=1.6];
  AWAKE    -> SLEEPSUP   [arrowhead=tee];
  CIRCOSC  -> MORNPEAK;
  MORNPEAK -> CF24;
  BOUT     -> SLEEPFRAG;
  SLEEPFRAG -> SLEEPDEB;
  SLEEPDEB -> CORTSUP    [arrowhead=tee, penwidth=1.4,
                          label="tired patients\nsuppress less"];
  AWAKE    -> AWAKEF;
  BOUT     -> AWAKEF;
  MUCUS    -> MORNPEAK   [label="overnight\naccumulation"];

  /* 13. P2X3 antagonists */
  GEFA     -> OCC3       [penwidth=1.5, color="#1565C0"];
  GEFA     -> OCC23      [penwidth=1.5, color="#E64A19",
                          label="SELECTIVITY ≈ 1 →\nSAME exposure hits both"];
  CAMLI    -> OCC3       [penwidth=1.5, color="#1565C0"];
  CAMLI    -> OCC23      [style=dashed, color="#BDBDBD",
                          label="1500x selective →\nnegligible at\ntherapeutic dose"];
  ELIA     -> OCC3       [color="#1565C0"];
  ELIA     -> OCC23      [style=dashed, color="#FFB74D", label="60x"];
  ELIA     -> DILI       [color="#E64A19", style=dashed,
                          label="idiosyncratic,\nNOT target-mediated"];
  SIVO     -> OCC3       [color="#1565C0", label="QD dosing →\ntrough coverage\nshortfall"];
  SIVO     -> OCC23      [style=dashed, color="#FFB74D", label="30x"];
  RENAL    -> GEFA       [arrowhead=tee, label="OAT3 clearance"];
  ATP_ASL  -> OCC3       [arrowhead=tee, penwidth=1.3, color="#795548",
                          label="ATP COMPETITION:\nmore airway ATP →\nless inhibition"];
  OCC3     -> P2X3       [arrowhead=tee, penwidth=2.0, color="#1565C0"];
  OCC3     -> CEILING;
  CEILING  -> TUSSDRIVE  [label="floor on achievable\ncough reduction"];
  TRPV1    -> CEILING    [label="P2X3-independent\narm"];
  TRPA1    -> CEILING;
  RAR      -> CEILING;

  /* 14. Central neuromodulators */
  GABAP    -> A2CH       [arrowhead=tee, penwidth=1.5, color="#3949AB"];
  GABAP    -> WINDUP     [arrowhead=tee, penwidth=1.4, color="#3949AB"];
  GABAP    -> GABAAE     [color="#E64A19"];
  PREGAB   -> A2CH       [arrowhead=tee, color="#3949AB"];
  PREGAB   -> GABAAE     [color="#E64A19"];
  MORPH    -> ENKEPH     [label="μ-agonism at\nthe same targets", color="#3949AB"];
  MORPH    -> DESCINH    [penwidth=1.6, color="#3949AB"];
  MORPH    -> NTS        [arrowhead=tee, penwidth=1.4, color="#3949AB"];
  MORPH    -> OPIOIDAE   [color="#E64A19"];
  NALBU    -> DESCINH    [color="#3949AB", label="κ-agonist"];
  NALBU    -> OPIOIDAE   [color="#E64A19", style=dashed];
  AMITRIP  -> DESCINH    [color="#3949AB", label="NA/5-HT re-uptake"];
  AMITRIP  -> NAV17      [arrowhead=tee, style=dashed];
  BACLO    -> TLESR      [arrowhead=tee, color="#3949AB"];
  BACLO    -> NTS        [arrowhead=tee, color="#3949AB"];
  DEXTRO   -> NMDA       [arrowhead=tee, style=dashed, color="#90A4AE",
                          label="weak in RCC"];
  CODEINE  -> NTS        [arrowhead=tee, style=dashed, color="#90A4AE",
                          label="no better than\nplacebo (negative\ncontrol)"];
  MOR_P    -> ENKEPH     [dir=back, style=dashed];

  /* 15. Treatable traits */
  ICS      -> EOS        [arrowhead=tee, penwidth=1.5, color="#2E7D32"];
  ICS      -> NFKB       [arrowhead=tee, color="#2E7D32"];
  ICS      -> FENO       [arrowhead=tee];
  LTRA     -> LTD4       [arrowhead=tee, color="#2E7D32"];
  BIOLOG   -> EOS        [arrowhead=tee, color="#2E7D32", style=dashed];
  PPI      -> ACIDREF    [arrowhead=tee, penwidth=1.4, color="#2E7D32"];
  PPI      -> NONACID    [style=dotted, color="#BDBDBD",
                          label="NO EFFECT — this is\nwhy PPI trials fail"];
  PROKIN   -> TLESR      [arrowhead=tee, color="#2E7D32"];
  ANTIHIST -> HIST       [arrowhead=tee, color="#2E7D32"];
  ANTIHIST -> EXTRAP     [arrowhead=tee, style=dashed];
  NASSTER  -> T_UACS     [arrowhead=tee, color="#2E7D32"];
  ACEISTOP -> BK         [arrowhead=tee, penwidth=1.6, color="#2E7D32"];
  AZITHRO  -> NEUT       [arrowhead=tee, color="#2E7D32"];

  /* 16. Non-pharmacological */
  SLT      -> CORTSUP    [penwidth=1.8, color="#00796B",
                          label="TRAINS the suppression\nnetwork: LCQ +1.5"];
  SLT      -> HABIT      [arrowhead=tee, color="#00796B"];
  CSTX     -> CORTSUP    [color="#00796B"];
  CBTC     -> HYPERVIG   [arrowhead=tee, penwidth=1.4, color="#00796B"];
  CBTC     -> DESCFAC    [arrowhead=tee, color="#00796B"];
  SLNBLOCK -> SLN        [arrowhead=tee, color="#00796B"];
  NEBLIDO  -> NAV17      [arrowhead=tee, color="#00796B",
                          label="use-dependent\nNa+ block, minutes"];
  VOCALHYG -> EPI_DAM    [arrowhead=tee, style=dashed, color="#00796B"];

  /* 17. On-target adverse effects */
  TASTEATP -> P2X23      [penwidth=1.5, label="ATP is THE taste\nneurotransmitter"];
  TASTEBUD -> TASTEATP;
  OCC23    -> P2X23      [arrowhead=tee, penwidth=1.8, color="#E64A19"];
  OCC23    -> DYSG       [penwidth=2.0, color="#E64A19",
                          label="the SAME occupancy curve\nthat gives efficacy"];
  DYSG     -> DISCONT    [penwidth=1.6, color="#E64A19"];
  DYSG     -> ADHERE     [arrowhead=tee, penwidth=1.6, color="#E64A19"];
  DISCONT  -> ADHERE     [arrowhead=tee, penwidth=1.5, color="#E64A19"];
  ADHERE   -> OCC3       [penwidth=1.6, color="#E64A19",
                          label="effectiveness\n< efficacy"];
  DILI     -> ELIA       [arrowhead=tee, style=dashed, color="#E64A19"];
  GABAAE   -> GABAP      [arrowhead=tee, style=dashed, color="#E64A19",
                          label="dose titration\nlimited"];
  OPIOIDAE -> MORPH      [arrowhead=tee, style=dashed, color="#E64A19"];

  /* 18. Measurement */
  TRPV1    -> CAPSC5     [label="capsaicin acts HERE —\nbypassing P2X3"];
  P2X3     -> ATPCHAL;
  ASIC3    -> CITRICA;
  TRPV1    -> CITRICA;
  BOUT     -> COUGHMON   [penwidth=1.6];
  EOS      -> SPUTUM;
  FENO     -> FENOM;
  ACIDREF  -> PHIMP;
  NONACID  -> PHIMP;
  COUGHMON -> CF24       [penwidth=1.8];
  COUGHMON -> CFAWK;
  OCC3     -> ATPCHAL    [arrowhead=tee, penwidth=1.7, color="#1565C0",
                          label="STRONG shift"];
  OCC3     -> CAPSC5     [arrowhead=tee, style=dotted, color="#90A4AE",
                          label="MINIMAL shift —\nthe class's diagnostic\nsignature"];

  /* 19. Endpoints */
  BOUT     -> CF24       [penwidth=1.8];
  AWAKEF   -> CFAWK      [penwidth=1.5];
  CF24     -> VAS        [penwidth=1.3];
  URGE     -> VAS        [penwidth=1.5,
                          label="PROs track the URGE,\nnot only the count"];
  URGE     -> CSD;
  CF24     -> CSD;
  CF24     -> LCQ        [arrowhead=tee];
  URGE     -> LCQ        [arrowhead=tee, penwidth=1.4];
  HYPERVIG -> LCQ        [arrowhead=tee];
  SLEEPFRAG -> LCQ       [arrowhead=tee];
  CF24     -> COMPLIC    [penwidth=1.4];
  COMPLIC  -> LCQ        [arrowhead=tee];
  COMPLIC  -> DEPRESS;
  DEPRESS  -> HYPERVIG   [penwidth=1.3];
  LCQ      -> RESPOND;
  CF24     -> RESPOND;
  CORTSUP  -> PLACEBO    [penwidth=1.5,
                          label="trial participation itself\ntrains suppression"];
  EPI_REP  -> PLACEBO    [label="natural resolution"];
  PLACEBO  -> CF24       [arrowhead=tee, penwidth=1.7, color="#AD1457",
                          label="≈ -30% at 12 weeks\nBEFORE any drug effect"];

  /* 20. Disease-state integrators — the bistable core */
  P2X3EXP  -> PERGAIN    [penwidth=1.5];
  PERIPHSENS -> PERGAIN  [penwidth=1.5];
  ECTOPIC  -> PERGAIN;
  WINDUP   -> CENGAIN    [penwidth=1.7];
  GABAI    -> CENGAIN    [arrowhead=tee, penwidth=1.4];
  MICROG   -> CENGAIN;
  DESCINH  -> CENGAIN    [arrowhead=tee, penwidth=1.5];
  PERGAIN  -> LOOPGAIN   [penwidth=1.7];
  CENGAIN  -> LOOPGAIN   [penwidth=1.7];
  LOOPGAIN -> HYPERSENS  [penwidth=1.8, color="#C62828"];
  HYPERSENS -> TUSSDRIVE [penwidth=1.7, color="#C62828"];
  HYPERSENS -> ECTOPIC   [penwidth=1.4];
  HYPERSENS -> CAPSC5    [arrowhead=tee, label="hypertussia"];
  HYPERSENS -> URGE      [penwidth=1.4, label="allotussia:\ntalking, laughing,\nperfume, cold air"];

  /* THE VICIOUS CIRCLE — drawn bold red */
  MECHSTR  -> EPI_DAM    [color="#D32F2F", penwidth=2.2, style=bold];
  ATP_ASL  -> AFIRE      [color="#D32F2F", penwidth=2.2, style=bold];
  AFIRE    -> WINDUP     [color="#D32F2F", penwidth=2.2, style=bold];
  WINDUP   -> TUSSDRIVE  [color="#D32F2F", penwidth=2.2, style=bold];
  CPG      -> EXPUL      [color="#D32F2F", penwidth=2.2, style=bold];

  /* Cross-links that matter clinically */
  EOS      -> ICS        [dir=back, style=dotted, color="#2E7D32",
                          label="FeNO/sputum eos\nSELECT the responder"];
  ACIDREF  -> PPI        [dir=back, style=dotted, color="#2E7D32",
                          label="pH-impedance\nSELECTS the responder"];
  ATP_ASL  -> GEFA       [dir=back, style=dotted, color="#1565C0",
                          label="high airway ATP →\nhigher dose needed"];
  T_POSTVIR -> LOOPGAIN  [style=dashed, penwidth=1.4,
                          label="loop gain decides:\nresolve vs become\nrefractory"];
  SLEEPSUP -> CF24       [arrowhead=tee, style=dashed,
                          label="why 24-h < awake rate"];

}
